\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Diagnostic distribution for the marginal AU\nobreakspace  {}Mic candidate: the per-window control-ring peak signal-to-noise ratios of all 225 windows of this release (histogram; median 4.51, 90th percentile 5.81), i.e.\ the distribution of maxima expected from noise plus background structure alone. The dashed line marks the formal $5\sigma $ crossing threshold; the solid line marks the on-source peak of the AU\nobreakspace  {}Mic candidate window ($5.97$, the 94.7th percentile of this distribution) and the dotted line its own control maximum ($5.85$). Twelve windows (5\%) have control maxima at or above the AU\nobreakspace  {}Mic on-source value. Three windows lie beyond the plotted range, marked at upper right: HD\nobreakspace  {}285968 Band\nobreakspace  {}6 at $10.9$, and $\beta $\nobreakspace  {}Pictoris Band\nobreakspace  {}6 at $9.1$ and at $15.2$, the latter the CO-filled control ring discussed in the text.}}{30}{figure.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:aumic}{{10}{30}{Diagnostic distribution for the marginal AU~Mic candidate: the per-window control-ring peak signal-to-noise ratios of all 225 windows of this release (histogram; median 4.51, 90th percentile 5.81), i.e.\ the distribution of maxima expected from noise plus background structure alone. The dashed line marks the formal $5\sigma $ crossing threshold; the solid line marks the on-source peak of the AU~Mic candidate window ($5.97$, the 94.7th percentile of this distribution) and the dotted line its own control maximum ($5.85$). Twelve windows (5\%) have control maxima at or above the AU~Mic on-source value. Three windows lie beyond the plotted range, marked at upper right: HD~285968 Band~6 at $10.9$, and $\beta $~Pictoris Band~6 at $9.1$ and at $15.2$, the latter the CO-filled control ring discussed in the text}{figure.10}{}}
